  return {"grade6":{"g6-main-w6-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab","number":12,"week":6,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Integrated Build-and-Check (Lab)","summary":"Students run a full build-and-check task across four stations, record accuracy and risk verdicts, decide whether to use the output, and diagnose their weakest strand.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Run a small integrated build-and-check task end-to-end and record the checks made.","Identify which strand most needs work before the signature solution.","Evaluate the final output for accuracy and risk before deciding to use it."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["This is your dress rehearsal. You will run a real task from start to finish - build it with a system and a prompt, then check it for accuracy and risk before deciding whether to use it. By the end you will know exactly which strand to sharpen before the signature solution."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run a build-and-check task through all four strands end-to-end.","I can record the accuracy and risk checks I made.","I can name which strand I most need to improve."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Build-and-check","definition":"Producing an AI solution and then testing it before use."},{"term":"Accuracy verdict","definition":"Whether the output is correct, incorrect, or unclear."},{"term":"Risk verdict","definition":"How risky the output is and what would reduce it."},{"term":"Mitigation","definition":"An action that reduces a risk."},{"term":"Weakest link","definition":"The strand most likely to fail under pressure."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Build, then check","body":["Building means choosing a suitable system and designing a clear [[prompt]] to reach a useful output.","Checking means triaging that output for accuracy and running a risk assessment before you decide to use it. Building without checking just produces confident mistakes."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Decide and diagnose","body":["Your final call is **use**, **do not use**, or **use-with-changes** - and you must justify it with your two verdicts.","Then diagnose your [[weakest link]]: the strand where your evidence was thinnest. That is your focus before the signature solution."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Run the four stations end-to-end. Build with a system and prompt, check for accuracy and risk, decide whether to use the output, and diagnose your weakest strand."],"items":["Name the system type and why it suits the task.","Design a clear, specific prompt.","Triage the curated output for accuracy.","Run a risk assessment and choose a mitigation.","Decide use / do not use / use-with-changes and diagnose your weakest strand."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Did your accuracy verdict or your risk verdict decide your use decision?","Which strand was your weakest link, and how will you strengthen it?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write your focus strand and one action to improve it before the signature solution.","Explain why building without checking is risky."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 6 - Lab - Worksheet | Integrated Build-and-Check (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"Record your evidence at each of the four stations.","stem":"System type + why:\nPrompt:\nAccuracy verdict + reason:\nRisk verdict + mitigation:","lookFor":"System choice justified by the task (e.g. a learning system that finds language patterns, suited because summarising needs pattern recognition rather than fixed rules), a specific prompt, an accuracy verdict with a reason that can be checked against the source, and a risk verdict whose mitigation matches the risk (e.g. main risk is using an unverified detail; mitigation is verify before use).","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Make your use decision and name your weakest strand with a reason.","stem":"Decision: use / do not use / use-with-changes because ...\nWeakest strand:\nAction to improve:","lookFor":"A justified decision that treats use-with-changes as a real third option rather than a yes/no, plus an honest and specific weakest-strand diagnosis justified by where the evidence was thinnest, with one concrete improvement action.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"Complete one row per station and finish with your decision.","stem":"Station / strand | Evidence produced | Verdict | Note for signature solution","lookFor":"All four stations completed with recorded evidence and a verdict for each, finishing with the use decision. Emerging completes all four strands with recorded evidence; approaching completes most stations with some evidence.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"State your use decision with a reason, and name the strand you most need to improve before the signature solution.","stem":"","lookFor":"The decision is tied back to the accuracy and risk verdicts rather than to how the output looks, and the named strand is specific enough to act on before the signature solution.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w6-lab-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Rewrite your prompt so the output would earn a lower risk verdict, and predict how the use decision would change.","stem":"","lookFor":"Rewritten prompt visibly reduces the risk named at station 4 and the prediction explains the shift in the use decision (e.g. from use-with-changes to use) - the stretch expectation, which may also include a written justification of the use-with-changes option.","autoMarked":false,"frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}},"g6-main-w7-core":{"id":"g6-main-w7-core","number":13,"week":7,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Signature Solution - Planning","summary":"Students plan a five-part signature solution - goal, prompt structure, inputs, evaluation method and risk plan - and take it through an approve-to-build gate.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Plan a structured AI solution: state the goal, the prompt structure, and the check steps.","Identify the inputs/data and the output-evaluation method.","Describe one risk and how the plan reduces it."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Today you become a designer, not just a prompter. Before anyone types a single word into an AI tool, you will plan a small solution with five parts that fit together: a goal, a prompt structure, inputs, a check, and a risk plan. A good plan is like a bridge design drawn before the first bolt is placed - it lets you find weak spots on paper, where fixing them is cheap."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can state the goal of my solution in one clear sentence.","I can lay out a prompt structure with a role, a task, and one rule.","I can name the inputs my solution needs and how I will check the output.","I can describe one risk and one way my plan reduces it."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Signature solution","definition":"A small, reusable AI design with a clear goal and connected parts that solves one simple task."},{"term":"Prompt structure","definition":"The shape of a prompt: a role for the AI, a clear task, and at least one rule or limit."},{"term":"Input","definition":"The information a prompt works on, chosen to contain no personal or identifying data."},{"term":"Evaluation method","definition":"The agreed way you will judge whether an output is accurate."},{"term":"Risk mitigation","definition":"A design choice that lowers the chance or impact of something going wrong."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"From one prompt to a whole solution","body":["In Grade 5 you improved a single prompt. This term you design a solution: a set of parts that work together to do one simple job well.","The five parts are the goal, the [[prompt structure]], the inputs, the [[evaluation method]], and the risk plan. If any part is missing, the solution is harder to trust."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Writing a prompt structure","body":["A [[prompt structure]] names a role ('You are a timetable helper'), a task ('list the three earliest buses'), and one rule ('if a time is missing, say so').","The role focuses the AI, the task says exactly what to do, and the rule keeps the output honest and easy to check."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Checks and risks before you build","body":["An [[evaluation method]] says how you will judge accuracy, such as comparing the output to a known-correct answer key.","A risk plan names one thing that could go wrong, like a confident wrong answer, and one design choice that reduces it, like a 'say if unsure' rule plus a human check. Never put personal or identifying data into a prompt."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will now plan your own signature solution on the plan sheet. You will not log in to any tool; the teacher runs any AI on the board. Your job is to make the plan complete and safe."],"items":["Read your task card and write the goal in one clear sentence.","Fill the role-task-rule slots for your prompt structure.","List the inputs your prompt needs, checking there is no personal data.","Write your evaluation method and one risk with its mitigation.","Self-check against the five-part list, then submit for the approve-to-build gate."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which part of a plan is easiest to forget, and why does that matter?","How does a 'say if unsure' rule make an output safer to trust?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the one part of your plan you are most confident about.","Write the one part you will strengthen before building next week."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 7 - Core - Worksheet | Signature Solution - Planning","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Name the five parts: using your task card, complete each part of the plan in one line.","stem":"The goal is to ___.\nThe AI acts as a ___ (role).\nThe task is to ___.\nOne rule is ___.\nThe inputs are ___ (no personal data).\nI will check accuracy by ___.\nOne risk is ___; my plan reduces it by ___.","lookFor":"All five parts are present: a goal naming the task and who it helps, a role + task + one rule structure, inputs with no personal or identifying data, a checkable evaluation method (e.g. compare labelled items to a teacher answer key), and one risk with a mitigation that clearly reduces that named risk. Evaluation and risk are the parts most often left blank or thin.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Spot the weak plan: read the two sample plans provided","stem":"The stronger plan is ___ because ___.","lookFor":"Chooses the complete plan and names a specific missing part - the evaluation method or the risk row - as the reason, rather than saying the plan is longer or neater. Structure beats size: a missing check is a hidden weak spot.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"My plan review record: fill one row for each of the five parts (plan part / what I wrote / ready? Y/N) and mark whether it is ready.","lookFor":"One row per part, each quoting what the student actually wrote plus an honest Y/N. Check the evaluation and risk rows hardest: a 'Y' there should sit beside a method that can really be checked and a mitigation tied to the named risk.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your goal sentence and the one risk your plan reduces.","lookFor":"Goal is one clear sentence saying what the solution does and who it helps. The risk is realistic (e.g. a confident but wrong answer) and is one the plan genuinely reduces through its rule, check or human step.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): add a second rule to your prompt structure and explain which kind of wrong answer it is designed to stop.","lookFor":"Writes a second rule that fits the same prompt structure and names the kind of wrong answer it blocks (e.g. a confident guess, a dropped item, an unclear label). The link between the rule and the error it stops is what to look for.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"}]}},"g6-main-w7-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab","number":14,"week":7,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Prototype and Pressure-Test the Plan (Lab)","summary":"Students prototype their approved plan on the board, break it on purpose with a tricky curated input, and design an if-then fallback branch that keeps a person in the loop.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Prototype the prompt structure and pressure-test the plan against a tricky input.","Add a fallback branch for when the output fails a check.","Record what changed and why after the pressure test."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["A plan on paper looks tidy. Today you find out how it behaves under pressure. You will build a quick prototype, then throw your hardest inputs at it on purpose - the missing item, the messy note, the two-in-one line. When it stumbles, you will not hide the failure; you will design a fallback branch that catches it safely. Engineers stress-test bridges before people cross them. You will stress-test your solution before it is trusted."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run my prompt structure on a normal input and read the output.","I can pressure-test it with a tricky input and spot where it fails.","I can add a fallback branch that says what to do when a check fails.","I can record the change I made and the reason for it."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Prototype","definition":"A first working version built quickly to see how a design really behaves."},{"term":"Pressure test","definition":"Deliberately trying a tricky input to reveal a weak spot."},{"term":"Edge case","definition":"An unusual input at the edge of what a solution expects, like a missing or double value."},{"term":"Fallback branch","definition":"A planned 'if a check fails, then...' response that handles a failure safely."},{"term":"Error type","definition":"A label for what went wrong: wrong, unclear, or missing."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Prototype first, judge second","body":["A [[prototype]] is a fast first version. Running it shows how your design behaves, not just how you hoped it would.","The teacher runs your prompt on the board with a normal curated input. You read the output and decide: did it meet the goal?"]},{"type":"text","heading":"Design the fallback branch","body":["When a check fails, a good solution follows a [[fallback branch]] instead of giving a confident wrong answer.","Write it as 'If the check fails, then ___ and ask a person.' Keeping a human in the loop is part of responsible design.","Remember: only curated, made-up inputs - never real names or personal data."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will prototype your approved plan, pressure-test it, and add a fallback branch. The teacher runs the AI on the board; you do not log in. Log every run."],"items":["Copy your prompt structure into the prototype slot of your log.","Watch the normal-input run on the board and record whether it met the goal.","Pressure-test with a tricky curated input and record the error type.","Write your fallback branch as an if-then sentence that asks a person.","Log the one change you made and the reason it will help."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which tricky input broke the most prototypes, and why?","Why is a handled failure safer than a confident wrong answer?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the weak spot your pressure test exposed.","Write how your fallback branch will handle it next week."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 7 - Lab - Worksheet | Prototype and Pressure-Test the Plan (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Predict then test: before the board run, predict how your prompt will handle one tricky input. After the run, record what actually happened.","stem":"I predict the output will be ___.\nThe actual output was ___.\nThe error type was ___ (wrong / unclear / missing).","lookFor":"The prediction is written before the run and the actual output after it, and the error type is one of the three labels. A real pressure test exposes something - e.g. 'found: charger and a scarf' returning 'devices' only is a missing error, not a wrong one.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Write your fallback branch: turn your exposed failure into a safe fallback using the if-then frame","stem":"If ___ then ___ and ask a person.","lookFor":"The branch handles the failure the pressure test actually exposed and keeps a person in the loop (e.g. 'if a notice names two items, then label each one separately, and if still unclear label it other and ask a person'). A vague branch, or one that does not match the observed failure, is only approaching.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Prototype build/test log: record each run - the input used (curated), the output, whether it met the goal (Y/N), and the error type if any.","lookFor":"At least one normal run and one pressure test are logged, each with its curated input, the output, a Y/N against the goal, and a classified error type for any run that failed. Logs without an error type are returned.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write the weak spot you found and the fallback branch you designed for it.","lookFor":"Names one specific weak spot from their own log, not a general worry, and gives a fallback branch that visibly answers that weak spot.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"},{"id":"g6-main-w7-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): design a second fallback for a different error type and say which failure is more likely and why.","lookFor":"A second branch aimed at a different error type (wrong / unclear / missing) from the first, plus a judgement about which failure is more likely with a reason drawn from the runs they logged.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"tierProbed":"emerging","evidenceType":"product"}]}},"g6-main-w8-core":{"id":"g6-main-w8-core","number":15,"week":8,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Signature Solution - Building","summary":"Students build their signature solution by following their approved plan, evaluate and flag every output, and log one evidence-based improvement as evaluate -> change -> result.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Build the solution by following the plan and prompt structure.","Evaluate outputs for accuracy and flag any that are incorrect or unclear.","Make at least one improvement based on an output check.","Keep personal and identifying data out of every prompt and keep a person in the loop for anything flagged."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Today you build for real. You will follow your approved plan, run your inputs, and look hard at every output - not just the ones that look right. When you find an answer that is wrong or unclear, you flag it, change one thing, and watch what happens. This is how real systems get better: one careful change, one honest result. Keep every prompt free of personal data, and keep a person in the loop for anything you flag."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can build my solution by following my approved plan.","I can evaluate outputs and flag ones that are wrong or unclear.","I can make one improvement and explain what changed and why.","I can keep personal data out of every prompt."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Build","definition":"Turning your approved plan into a working solution by following it step by step."},{"term":"Evaluate","definition":"Judging an output against your check to decide if it is correct and clear."},{"term":"Flag","definition":"Marking an output that is wrong or unclear so it gets attention and a fix."},{"term":"Improvement","definition":"One deliberate change made in response to an evaluation."},{"term":"Iteration loop","definition":"The evaluate -> change -> result cycle that makes a solution better over time."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Follow the plan, do not improvise","body":["Building means running your approved prompt structure on defined inputs, not inventing new prompts on the spot.","Record each output before you change anything. That way you can see what your solution really does."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Evaluate, flag, improve","body":["Evaluate each output against your check: correct, unclear, or wrong. Flag anything that fails.","Then make one improvement and re-run. Record it as **evaluate -> change -> result** so the cause of the improvement is clear."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will build your solution from your approved plan, evaluate the outputs, flag errors, and log one improvement. The teacher runs the AI on the board; you do not log in."],"items":["Restate your goal and check on your log.","Run your prompt structure on defined curated inputs and record each output.","Evaluate each output and flag the wrong or unclear ones.","Make one improvement in response to a flag and re-run it.","Log the loop as evaluate -> change -> result."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["How did you tell a subtly wrong output from a correct one?","Why is one change at a time better than many at once?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the one improvement you made and why.","Write what you would evaluate more carefully next time."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 8 - Core - Worksheet | Signature Solution - Building","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Flag the errors: read the five curated outputs provided. Mark each correct, unclear, or wrong and flag the ones that fail the check.","stem":"Output ___ is ___ (correct / unclear / wrong) because ___.","lookFor":"Judges each output against the known-correct reference rather than a hunch, catches both seeded errors among the correct-looking rows, and gives a reason tied to the check (for example, 'other' for a tablet charger is wrong because it should be 'devices').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Log one improvement: choose one flagged output and record your improvement using the loop frame.","stem":"Evaluate: ___.\nChange: ___.\nResult: ___.","lookFor":"One change only, made in response to a specific flag, with the observed result recorded - for example 'Evaluate: charger mislabelled. Change: added a devices examples rule. Result: charger now devices, accuracy up.' Cause and effect should be visible in the loop.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Build and improvement log: record each output, your judgement, whether you flagged it, and the improvement you made. Use the columns Input (curated), Output, Judgement, Improvement made.","lookFor":"The build follows the approved plan and prompt structure with defined, curated inputs rather than improvised prompts; every row is evaluated and flagged rather than only the obvious ones; all inputs are free of personal or identifying data.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your one improvement as evaluate -> change -> result.","lookFor":"All three parts of the loop are present and connected, showing the change was driven by an evaluation and that the result was actually observed, not assumed.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): make a second improvement and use your log to say which change raised accuracy more, with evidence.","lookFor":"Compares the two changes using evidence from the log rather than impression, and recognises that one change at a time is what makes the comparison possible.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"}]}},"g6-main-w8-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab","number":16,"week":8,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Extended Build and Evaluation (Lab)","summary":"Students complete their solution, run it across a six-input curated test set to report an accuracy count, handle a failure gracefully with their fallback, and finish with a three-question risk check.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Complete a working solution and evaluate its outputs across several test inputs.","Handle an incorrect output gracefully and document the fix.","Run a basic risk check and confirm no personal data is used."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["This is the finish line for your signature solution - but finishing is not just getting one right answer. Today you prove it works by running it across several test inputs and counting how many it gets right. When one fails, your fallback catches it gracefully and you document the fix. Finally you run a basic risk check: is it accurate, is it clear, and is any prompt free of personal data? A solution you can measure and defend is one people can trust."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can complete a working solution that follows my plan.","I can evaluate its outputs across several test inputs and measure accuracy.","I can handle an incorrect output gracefully using my fallback.","I can run a basic risk check and document the fix I made."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Test set","definition":"A small, curated group of inputs, including edge cases, used to measure how a solution performs."},{"term":"Accuracy count","definition":"The number of correct outputs out of the total tested, such as 5 out of 6."},{"term":"Graceful handling","definition":"Using the fallback so an incorrect output is caught safely, not presented as final."},{"term":"Documented fix","definition":"A written record of the change made to correct a failure and its effect."},{"term":"Risk check","definition":"A quick review of accuracy, clarity, and data safety before a solution is trusted."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Prove it across several inputs","body":["One correct answer is not proof. Run your finished solution across a **test set** of several curated inputs and count how many outputs are correct.","Report accuracy as a simple count, like 5 out of 6, so your claim is honest and checkable."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Handle failures and check the risks","body":["When an output is wrong, let your fallback catch it and keep a person in the loop, then document the fix and its effect.","Finish with a basic risk check: accurate enough? clear enough? any personal data used? The data answer must always be no, because we use only curated inputs."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["You will complete your solution, evaluate it across six curated inputs, handle any failure with your fallback, document the fix, and run a basic risk check. The teacher runs the AI on the board; you do not log in."],"items":["Confirm your build follows the plan and the fallback is wired in.","Define what counts as a correct output.","Run all six curated inputs and record each result.","Compute accuracy and handle any failure with your fallback, documenting the fix.","Complete the three-question risk check and note the biggest remaining risk."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Why is an accuracy count across several inputs fairer than judging one output?","What is the biggest remaining risk in your solution, and who should check it?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write your accuracy result and the fix you documented.","Write one thing your risk check made you notice."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 8 - Lab - Worksheet | Extended Build and Evaluation (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Run and count: record the result of each of the six curated test inputs, mark correct or not, and compute your accuracy count.","stem":"Input ___ output ___ is ___ (correct / not).\nMy accuracy is ___ out of 6.","lookFor":"Accuracy is stated as a count across the whole test set (for example 5 out of 6), judged against a definition of a correct output agreed before testing - not a claim based on one lucky case.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Document the fix and risk check: record how your fallback handled a failure, the fix you made, and your three-question risk check.","stem":"The fallback handled ___ by ___.\nMy fix was ___ and the result was ___.\nRisk check - accurate? ___ clear? ___ personal data used? no.","lookFor":"Graceful handling means the fallback caught the failure and kept a person in the loop rather than the wrong output being deleted or presented as final; the fix is traceable with its effect recorded; all three risk questions are answered and the personal-data answer is no because every input is curated.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Test-set evaluation and risk record: fill one row per test input with its result, then complete the risk-check summary below. Use the columns Input (curated), Output, Correct? (Y/N), Note / fix.","lookFor":"A completed solution that follows the plan with the fallback wired in, evaluated across all six inputs with an accuracy count, and a risk-check summary covering accuracy, clarity and data safety.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your accuracy count and confirm your risk check found no personal data.","lookFor":"States accuracy as correct out of total and confirms explicitly that no personal or identifying data was used, linking that to the inputs being curated.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"},{"id":"g6-main-w8-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): add a seventh harder edge case, predict the result, test it, and say whether your solution generalised and why.","lookFor":"Makes a prediction before testing, compares it with the actual result, and reasons about whether the solution handles inputs it has not seen - naming rare unseen edge cases as a remaining risk.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging"}]}},"g6-main-w9-core":{"id":"g6-main-w9-core","number":17,"week":9,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Signature Solution - Refining & Finishing","summary":"Students judge their signature solution against accuracy, usefulness and risk, then make one improvement and prove with re-testing that it helped.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Finish the solution so it meets the agreed success criteria.","Evaluate it for accuracy, usefulness and risk.","Explain one change that improved it."],"sections":[{"type":"text","heading":"Overview","body":["You are almost there. This week you become the judge of your own work, checking it for accuracy, usefulness and risk, then making one smart change that you can prove made it better."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can finish my solution so it meets the success criteria our class agreed on.","I can judge my solution for accuracy, usefulness and risk using the rubric.","I can explain one change I made and say why it made the solution better."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Refine","definition":"To improve something on purpose by comparing it to your goals."},{"term":"Accuracy","definition":"How often the system gives the right or sensible answer."},{"term":"Usefulness","definition":"How much the solution really helps the user do their task."},{"term":"Risk","definition":"What could go wrong or who could be harmed, including privacy."},{"term":"Evidence","definition":"Proof from testing, not just an opinion."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Judging your solution three ways","body":["A good builder does not just ask 'do I like it?'. You measure your work against the criteria the class agreed.","**Accuracy**: test with examples where you know the right answer. **Usefulness**: check it helps your real user. **Risk**: ask what could go wrong and whether any private data is exposed."]},{"type":"text","heading":"One change, proven","body":["You do not need many changes. Choose the one improvement that matters most to your user.","Make the change, then re-test. If accuracy went up and nothing else broke, you have evidence it worked. Write it in your refinement note."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Work with your partner. Judge your solution against the rubric, choose one improvement, make it, and prove it helped."],"items":["Read the three lenses on the criteria card.","Run one accuracy test with known answers and record the score.","Check usefulness against your real user's task.","Do a basic risk check for harm, fairness and privacy.","Pick one improvement, make it, and re-test.","Swap for 'two stars and a wish' feedback."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which lens was hardest to judge, and why?","How did re-testing change your confidence in your solution?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the one change you made and the evidence it helped.","Name one risk you are now sure your solution avoids."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 9 - Core - Worksheet | Signature Solution - Refining & Finishing","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w9-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Three-lens evaluation: judge your solution on each lens. Give a score or a yes/no and the evidence behind it.","stem":"Accuracy: I tested ___ and got ___\nUsefulness: it helps my user because ___\nRisk: I checked ___ so ___","lookFor":"Judges all three lenses with evidence from testing: known-answer test cases rather than opinion for accuracy, a usefulness judgement linked to the real user's task, and a harm, fairness or privacy risk that was actually checked.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"One improvement, proven: describe the single change you made and show before and after evidence.","stem":"The change I made was ___\nBefore: ___ After: ___\nNothing else broke because ___","lookFor":"One targeted change (a fixed or added rule, or cleaner example data) with before/after evidence, and a re-test confirming it helped without breaking another case.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Refinement log: record each check, your judgement and the evidence.","stem":"Lens | Judgement | Evidence | Action taken","lookFor":"All three lenses logged, each with a judgement, the evidence it came from, and the action taken; evidence traces back to testing rather than opinion.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: what one change improved your solution most, and how do you know?","lookFor":"Meets the Emerging criteria: names an accuracy, usefulness or risk judgement and one improvement.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): compare two possible improvements and justify, with evidence, why you chose one over the other.","lookFor":"Justifies why the chosen improvement beats a second candidate improvement, using evidence.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}},"g6-main-w9-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab","number":18,"week":9,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Final Iteration and Risk Review (Lab)","summary":"Students make their final improvement, sort risks on a likelihood-by-seriousness matrix, confirm the solution is safe and fair, and freeze the evaluated version for showcase.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Run a final evaluation across accuracy, usefulness and risk, and act on one improvement.","Complete a risk review and confirm the solution is safe and fair to use.","Document the final iteration with before-and-after evidence."],"sections":[{"type":"text","heading":"Overview","body":["Time for the final polish. In this Lab you make your last improvement, then act like a safety checker, running a full risk review so you can promise your solution is safe and fair before showcase."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run a final evaluation across accuracy, usefulness and risk and act on one improvement.","I can complete a risk review and confirm my solution is safe and fair.","I can record my final iteration with clear before-and-after evidence."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Iteration","definition":"One more round of improving and re-testing."},{"term":"Likelihood","definition":"How likely a risk is to actually happen."},{"term":"Seriousness","definition":"How much harm a risk would cause if it happened."},{"term":"Risk matrix","definition":"A grid that sorts risks by likelihood and seriousness."},{"term":"Freeze","definition":"To stop changing the version you have evaluated."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Sorting risks the smart way","body":["Not every risk is equal. A risk that is both likely and serious needs action now. A rare but very serious risk still needs a plan.","Place each risk on the [[risk matrix]], then decide: fix it now, or watch it. Always confirm no personal data is anywhere in your solution."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Finish, then freeze","body":["Make your final planned change and re-test with known answers. Record before and after so others can trust your evidence.","Then **freeze** the version. The solution you show at the carousel must be the exact one you tested and judged safe."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["With your partner, make the final change, re-test, run the full risk review, and freeze your solution ready for showcase."],"items":["Set your Lab goal from the refinement log.","Make the final planned improvement.","Re-test with at least five known-answer cases and record before and after.","List risks and place each on the matrix.","Decide actions and confirm no personal data is used.","Write a safe-and-fair statement and freeze the version."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which risk surprised you most when you placed it on the matrix?","How did freezing change how carefully you tested?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write your safe-and-fair statement in one sentence.","Name the risk you are most confident you have managed."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 9 - Lab - Worksheet | Final Iteration and Risk Review (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Risk matrix: list three risks and place each by likelihood and seriousness, then decide an action.","stem":"Risk 1: ___ likelihood ___ seriousness ___ action ___\nRisk 2: ___\nRisk 3: ___","lookFor":"Places risks by likelihood and seriousness and decides actions; look for both likelihood and seriousness reasoning, and note that a rare risk can still be serious enough to need a plan.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Final iteration evidence: record your last change and the before-and-after test results.","stem":"Final change: ___\nBefore: ___ After: ___\nSafe-and-fair statement: ___","lookFor":"The final change is shown with before/after numbers from re-testing, and the safe-and-fair statement covers both privacy and fairness.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Final iteration log: log each risk, its matrix position, the action, and confirm privacy.","stem":"Risk | Likelihood | Seriousness | Action / privacy check","lookFor":"Each risk carries a matrix position and an action, and the log confirms no personal data is used anywhere in the solution.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: write your safe-and-fair statement and one risk you managed with evidence.","lookFor":"Meets the Emerging criteria: confirms no personal data is used and that the solution is fair, and names one risk acted on with evidence.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w9-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): redesign one part of your solution so a high risk moves to a lower box on the matrix, and justify the change.","lookFor":"Proposes a design change that would move a risk to a lower box on the matrix, and justifies it.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}}}};
}

